---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import GuideTable from '../../components/GuideTable.astro';
import { bySlug, MONTHS, MONTH_SHORT } from '../../lib/data';

const ALL = MONTHS.map((_, i) => i);
const andaman = ['phuket', 'krabi'].map((s) => bySlug.get(s)!);
const gulf = ['koh-samui', 'koh-phangan'].map((s) => bySlug.get(s)!);
const avg = (ds: typeof andaman, m: number) => ds.reduce((a, d) => a + d.months[m].score, 0) / ds.length;
// Which coast has the better weather each month (by the average of our scores).
const label = { andaman: 'Andaman coast', gulf: 'Gulf of Thailand', both: 'Both are similar' } as const;
const better = ALL.map((m) => {
  const a = avg(andaman, m);
  const g = avg(gulf, m);
  const side: keyof typeof label = Math.abs(a - g) < 5 ? 'both' : a > g ? 'andaman' : 'gulf';
  return { m, side };
});
---

<Guide slug="thailand-islands-andaman-vs-gulf" photo="krabi">
  <p>
    Thailand has two island coasts with opposite rainy seasons. The <strong>Andaman coast</strong> on the west — Phuket, Krabi,
    Koh Phi Phi, Koh Lanta and Koh Lipe — is best from <strong>November to April</strong> and gets the south-west monsoon from
    May to October. The <strong>Gulf of Thailand</strong> on the east — Koh Samui, Koh Phangan and Koh Tao — is driest from{' '}
    <strong>February to August</strong> and wettest from October to December. So whatever month you travel, one coast is
    usually in good shape.
  </p>

  <h2>Weather rating by month</h2>
  <GuideTable caption="Weather rating for Thailand's Andaman and Gulf islands by month" months={ALL} rows={[
    { slug: 'phuket', label: 'Phuket (Andaman)' },
    { slug: 'krabi', label: 'Krabi & Phi Phi (Andaman)' },
    { slug: 'koh-samui', label: 'Koh Samui (Gulf)' },
    { slug: 'koh-phangan', label: 'Koh Phangan & Koh Tao (Gulf)' },
  ]} />
  <p class="small muted">Our ratings combine average temperature and rainfall from Thai Meteorological Department normals.</p>

  <h2>Rainfall by month</h2>
  <GuideTable caption="Average monthly rainfall on Thailand's islands" months={ALL} show="rain" rows={[
    { slug: 'phuket', label: 'Phuket (Andaman)' },
    { slug: 'koh-samui', label: 'Koh Samui (Gulf)' },
  ]} />

  <h2>Which coast for which month?</h2>
  <ul class="cols">
    {better.map(({ m, side }) => <li><b>{MONTH_SHORT[m]}:</b> {label[side]}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>The Andaman coast (November–April)</h2>
  <p>
    From November the north-east monsoon brings dry, sunny weather and calm, clear water to the west coast. December to March is
    the high season, with the best diving around the Similan Islands, which close to boats from mid-May to mid-October. From May,
    the south-west monsoon brings heavy showers, rough seas and strong currents on west-facing beaches — red flags are common, and
    some smaller islands such as Koh Lipe and Koh Phi Phi have fewer boats. Prices drop sharply, though, and many days still have
    long sunny spells. See <a href="/destinations/phuket/">Phuket</a> and <a href="/destinations/krabi/">Krabi</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Gulf of Thailand (February–August)</h2>
  <p>
    The Gulf islands are sheltered from the south-west monsoon, so they stay mostly dry through the summer, when the Andaman
    coast is wet. That makes Koh Samui, Koh Phangan and Koh Tao Thailand's best beach choice from June to August. Their rainy
    season comes later, from October to December, peaking in November, when ferries to Koh Tao can be cancelled. See{' '}
    <a href="/destinations/koh-samui/">Koh Samui</a> and <a href="/destinations/koh-phangan/">Koh Phangan &amp; Koh Tao</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>January–April</b> is the only stretch when both coasts are usually good — perfect for combining them, with a flight or a bus and ferry across the peninsula.</li>
    <li><b>Songkran</b>, the Thai New Year water festival (13–15 April), is celebrated on every island.</li>
    <li>The Full Moon Party on Koh Phangan happens every month, rain or shine.</li>
    <li>For the rest of the country, see the <a href="/best-time-to-visit-thailand/">best time to visit Thailand</a> and the <a href="/guides/monsoon-season-asia/">monsoon guide</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>

<style>
  .cols {
    columns: 2;
    column-gap: 24px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .cols {
      columns: 3;
    }
  }
</style>
